+++ b/docs/api/aurora-atmosphere.md
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Aurora atmosphere.1 — local experimental extension
+
+Opt-in API `0.1-aurora-atmosphere.1`, built on `0.1-aurora-shadow.2`.
+Stock Horizon rejects it. This is a local renderer extension, not a published upstream API.
+Existing API lines keep their shader inputs and rendering policy.
+
+```toml
+api = "0.1-aurora-atmosphere.1"
+[sun_shadows]
+quality = "high"
+[atmosphere]
+custom_celestials = true
+custom_clouds = true
+```
+
+As in shadow.2, a material stage and explicit shadow quality are required; the water
+environment contract also requires a post stage. The atmosphere table is optional;
+both switches default to false. Custom celestials require a sky stage. Unknown fields
+and atmosphere ownership on an earlier API are rejected at manifest validation.
+
+`custom_celestials` omits the native sun/moon textured quads in the Overworld sky.
+`custom_clouds` omits the native cloud draw in Overworld gameplay. Native stars, the
+below-horizon dark disc, title panorama, Nether and End policies remain as before.
+The pack supplies its replacement sky bodies and cloud rendering. Disabling a
+pack or selecting a legacy pack restores the normal layer policy.
+
+The shared frame appends `atmosphere: vec4<f32>` after the existing `water` field:
+the legacy fields occupy bytes 0..400, water starts at 400, atmosphere starts at 416,
+and the extended uniform is 432 bytes. `atmosphere.x` is the game world's lunar
+phase, `floor(day_time / 24000) mod 8`, with 0 full and 4 new; y/z/w are reserved.
+The renderer allocates the larger buffer for all packs; earlier WGSL structs are unchanged.
+
+Post stages additionally bind the existing native shadow receiver at group 2,
+with the same depth image, comparison sampler and 80-byte uniform used by materials.
+There is no extra shadow map allocation or caster pass. `sun_volume_visibility(p)`
+performs one comparison at camera-relative world position `p`, with edge/range fading.
+It returns 1 outside the map and when disabled. `sun_shadow.parameters.w` lets a pack
+skip scattering when the map is inactive (Low, night, unsupported dimension).
+Material PCF filtering retains its shadow.2 contract.
+
+This API does not provide multiple scattering, cloud shadows on terrain, temporal
+cloud accumulation, half-resolution post passes, or depth for transparent particles.
+The pack still owns integration and composition. Post stages run after world rendering
+and before the hand/HUD; depth is the world's reversed scene depth. In particular,
+cloud composition cannot sort independently against transparent geometry absent from
+that depth. The original `scene_color` is unchanged by earlier post stages, so a bloom
+pass that recombines with it must precede cloud/ray composition.
+
+Validation includes legacy API tests, all three shader backends, extended uniform layout,
+and a required-GPU test using the actual NativePost pipeline: an opaque caster must
+occlude, a cutout must transmit, disabled/Low must return full visibility, and both water
+and lunar phase fields must survive the upload. Run real GPU tests with
+`AURORA_REQUIRE_GPU=1 <render-test-binary> gfx::native_shadow::gpu_tests --test-threads=1`.
